      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "By the Trivial Inequality, we have $x^2 + y^2 \\ge 2xy$, so\n\\[\\frac{(x + y)^2}{x^2 + y^2} \\le \\frac{(x + y)^2}{2xy}.\\]By AM-GM,\n\\[\\frac{(x + y)^2}{2xy} = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{(x + y)^2 - 4xy}{2xy} \\le \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{(x + y - 2\\sqrt{xy})^2}{2xy}.\\]Notice that any of $\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2}$, $\\frac{(x + y - 2\\sqrt{xy})^2}{2xy}$ are equal to $\\frac{3}{2}$ (which occur when $x = y = 2\\sqrt{2}$), so the maximum is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}$.\n(The maximum is achieved when $x = y = 3$.) The answer is \\frac{3}{2}",
